+## Native tasks and compaction
+
+The launcher exports `CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TODO_TOOLS=1` and
+`CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TASKS=1`, including when an inherited shell set them to
+`0` or `false`. This exposes modern native task tools for custom gateway models;
+it does not override explicit tool restrictions or set a shared task-list ID.
+A caller's `CLAUDE_CODE_TASK_LIST_ID`, if explicitly supplied, is retained.
+
+`claudex-context.md` and Claude-only global instructions require inspecting the
+existing list before work, creating missing tasks, keeping progress/blockers
+current, and completing tasks only after verification. Resume and compaction
+continue existing task IDs rather than creating duplicates. Wrapper-owned
+SessionStart and UserPromptSubmit hooks reinforce that lifecycle. The hooks
+supply context only: they do not create tasks, write native task storage, or
+block session exit. If task tools are unavailable, the assistant must disclose
+that and label any text checklist as a fallback. `Ctrl+T` toggles the native
+list when tasks exist.
+
+The native default is `--autocompact 900000`. Explicit split and equals-form
+values, including `auto`, win. These launcher changes take effect on the next
+invocation, including a resumed session, not retroactively in a running process.
+No restart or compaction is performed by installing the change. Fixture tests
+verify arguments and hook output; actual new-session task updates and native
+`/autocompact` behavior remain separate live checks.
+
+## Bare launch and session resume
+
+With no arguments, an interactive launch inside Zellij offers:
+
+```text
+Resume session '<calling-pane-tab-name>'? [y/N]
+```
+
+The lookup matches the calling `ZELLIJ_PANE_ID`, ignoring plugin panes and other
+focused tabs. Answer `y` or `yes` (case-insensitive) to pass the exact name as one
+native `--resume=<name>` argument. No, empty input, unrecognized input or EOF
+continues ordinary launch; Ctrl+C cancels before credentials or services are
+touched. It does not auto-rename sessions, scan a custom session index, or retry
+a failed native resume as a new session. Native Claude resolves the name, so a
+missing session is reported by Claude rather than silently replaced.
+
+Any explicit argument bypasses both the optional lookup and the prompt:
+
+```bash
+claudex --resume my-other-session
+claudex --resume "my session with spaces"
+claudex --continue
+claudex --autocompact auto
+```
+
+The suggestion also skips safely outside Zellij, without terminal input/output
+and stderr, or when pane metadata is missing, ambiguous or unusable. Control
+and invisible formatting characters in metadata are rejected before display.
+The optional `zellij`/`timeout` lookup has a two-second timeout and a one-second
+kill grace; missing commands or lookup failure do not prevent ordinary launch.
+The existing `claudex` alias already points at this launcher; no reinstall is
+needed.
 
